# Location of project-specific Vanessa scenarios

> RULES — mandatory agreement on where to store a project's feature files and how to reference them from task documentation.

## Purpose

This rule separates:

- universal library steps and Vanessa runtime templates;
- project-specific scenarios for a particular database/project.

## MUST

| Requirement | Description |
|------------|-------------|
| Project feature files in `vanessa-tests/` | Project-specific scenarios MUST be stored in `<project_root>/vanessa-tests/features` |
| Project support files nearby | Project-specific support/fixtures MUST be stored in `<project_root>/vanessa-tests/support` |
| Links in task documentation | If a feature file was created or modified within a task, the task documentation MUST include a link to that file |
| Don’t mix with shared templates | Project-specific scenarios must not be stored in the shared runtime/template directory of the framework |

## Separation

### Shared / universal

- `framework/runtime/vanessa/*.json`
- Vanessa library steps in the tools directory

### Project-local

- `<project_root>/vanessa-tests/features`
- `<project_root>/vanessa-tests/support`

## What counts as a link in task documentation

A direct link or an explicit path to the created/updated `.feature` file is sufficient so the next agent can quickly open the scenario without re-searching.

